Subject: dxgi: keep painting composition targets from the comp buffer

Restores patch 0041's WM_PAINT behaviour on top of the d2d1-dcomp-11.14 base,
which replaced that block with "forward to the app's original wndproc first,
then re-blit the comp buffer afterwards".

Upstream's version exists to fix paint-driven plugins (an EPROM WebView2 loader
that only re-renders on WM_SIZE/WM_PAINT), and the trailing re-blit is meant to
restore the composed content the app's paint just erased. On Live that does not
hold: the erase is visible before the re-blit lands, so the sibling software
frame shows through on every paint and the pane flickers continuously. The same
configuration on the 11.13 base, where 0041's block is in place, does not
flicker - confirmed by A/B on one prefix and one set.

Painting straight from the comp buffer keeps the published DComp visual on
screen, which is what the DWM would show on Windows. When the buffer fails
0030's currency check the window is validated without blitting rather than
forwarded, so a stale-sized buffer is never stretched over the window.

This trades away upstream's paint-driven-plugin fix. If that turns out to
matter for a plugin we care about, the shape of a proper fix is to re-blit
synchronously within the same paint cycle rather than after EndPaint - but
that needs a repro of the plugin case to develop against.

diff --git a/dlls/dxgi/factory.c b/dlls/dxgi/factory.c
index 9c60a65bb9..5a9db821e9 100644
--- a/dlls/dxgi/factory.c
+++ b/dlls/dxgi/factory.c
@@ -766,37 +766,39 @@ static LRESULT CALLBACK dcomp_target_wndproc(HWND hwnd, UINT msg, WPARAM wparam,
 
         case WM_PAINT:
         {
-            /* Forward WM_PAINT to the app's original wndproc FIRST.  DComp
-             * plugins whose UI is paint-driven (EPROM's WebView2 loader only
-             * re-renders on WM_SIZE/WM_PAINT, not on a timer) otherwise never
-             * get their invalidation callback: hover/click state changes call
-             * InvalidateRect, the generated WM_PAINT was swallowed here, and
-             * the UI stayed frozen until the next resize forced a WM_SIZE
-             * redraw.  The app's paint may trigger a re-render + Present,
-             * which updates the comp buffer as a side effect.  Its own
-             * BeginPaint sends WM_ERASEBKGND, which this subclass still
-             * suppresses (returns 1), so no background erase happens.
-             *
-             * Afterwards re-blit the comp buffer via GetDC (NOT BeginPaint:
-             * the app's EndPaint already validated the update region, so a
-             * second BeginPaint would return an empty clip region and eat
-             * our blit) so the swapchain content stays on top of whatever
-             * the app painted. */
-            if (orig)
-                CallWindowProcW(orig, hwnd, msg, wparam, lparam);
-            else
-                DefWindowProcW(hwnd, msg, wparam, lparam);
-
+            /* Patch 0041: always paint from the comp buffer, however long
+             * the app has been idle.  It is the published DComp visual
+             * (Windows parity), and forwarding to the orig wndproc erases the
+             * surface and lets the sibling software frame show through - the
+             * Learn View revert ~3s after the last present, and a visible
+             * flicker on every paint on the 11.14 base.  Upstream forwards
+             * first and re-blits afterwards, which is meant to cover this, but
+             * measured on Live the erase wins often enough to flicker.  When
+             * the buffer fails the 0030 currency check, validate without
+             * blitting rather than forward. */
             {
-                static unsigned int paint_count;
-                ++paint_count;
-                if (paint_count <= 5 || !(paint_count % 200))
-                    FIXME("WM_PAINT #%u (forwarded): hwnd %p, comp_dc=%p.\n",
-                            paint_count, hwnd,
-                            (HDC)GetPropW(hwnd, L"__wine_dcomp_comp_dc"));
+                PAINTSTRUCT ps;
+                HDC comp_dc = (HDC)GetPropW(hwnd, L"__wine_dcomp_comp_dc");
+                LPARAM dims = (LPARAM)GetPropW(hwnd, L"__wine_dcomp_comp_size");
+
+                BeginPaint(hwnd, &ps);
+                if (comp_dc && dims
+                        && dcomp_comp_buffer_current(hwnd, LOWORD(dims), HIWORD(dims)))
+                {
+                    unsigned int w = LOWORD(dims);
+                    unsigned int h = HIWORD(dims);
+
+                    BitBlt(ps.hdc, 0, 0, w, h, comp_dc, 0, 0, SRCCOPY);
+                    {
+                        static unsigned int paint_count;
+                        ++paint_count;
+                        if (paint_count <= 5 || !(paint_count % 200))
+                            FIXME("WM_PAINT #%u: hwnd %p %ux%u, comp_dc=%p.\n",
+                                    paint_count, hwnd, w, h, comp_dc);
+                    }
+                }
+                EndPaint(hwnd, &ps);
             }
-            dcomp_reblit_comp_buffer(hwnd, "paint");
-            ValidateRect(hwnd, NULL);
             return 0;
         }
 
